<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manishtushu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manishtushu was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a> in the twenty-third century BCE, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon of Akkad</a>. He campaigned across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a> and is known from an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obelisk">obelisk</a> recording large land purchases. Like his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rimush">Rimush</a>, he is reported to have been assassinated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manishtushu.jpg" alt="Manishtushu" width="284" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shonagon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_de_Manishtusu_-_Sb_47_-_Antiquit%C3%A9s_orientales_du_Louvre.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
